  "hints": [
    "Two attributes: <code>axis=global</code> on <code>%b</code>, <code>axis=local</code> on <code>%t</code>.",
    "The offset <code>b·16 + t</code> is already a unique number: 16 is more than 15, the most <code>t</code> can add.",
    "The result doesn't change, only how it would run: 4 blocks of 16 threads."
  ],
  "explain": "On a GPU each value of <code>%b</code> is a block and each value of <code>%t</code> a thread in it. The offset <code>16b + t</code> gives every thread of every block its own element, which the rule checks as a mixed-radix number. <code>run</code> and the CPU render treat it as the same loops as before, so the bits can't change."
